<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!-- CHRN-60's step-1 spike, and NOTHING ELSE EVER.

         This manifest is the `debug` source set, so the receiver below does not
         exist in a release build at all. That is the whole reason it lives here
         rather than behind a runtime flag: an exported receiver that can start a
         recording is not something to ship and then remember to remove.

         The spike has to answer four things before the rest of the ticket is
         worth building — how much audio an unflushed writer loses, whether an
         app kill tears the file or the platform finalises it, whether a pause
         leaves one logical Ogg stream, and whether a PAUSED recorder still
         reports a recording configuration (which is the only resume signal
         available at minSdk 30). None of those is answerable without a real
         device, and none is answerable through the UI, which does not exist yet.

         Delete this directory when the spike's numbers are on the ticket. -->
    <application>
        <receiver
            android:name=".capture.SpikeReceiver"
            android:exported="true"/>
    </application>
</manifest>
